Z||000000||AkursedX||08-02-2001||11:08 PM||||Ok, well my 88GT came with a rear sway bar, and I assumed it came as part of the GT package.  Now I get my 87GT, and I see it has no rear sway bar.  So I'm confused now.<P>I am assuming the rear sway bar came as part of the WS6 package.  So, if it did, then GT's had the WS6 package as an option?  And if it did, then I am assuming I have a non-WS6 suspension.<P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||08-02-2001||11:19 PM||||Rear sway bars only came on <B>88</B> GT and Formula. It was not standard or optional on any other year.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AkursedX||08-02-2001||11:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>Rear sway bars only came on [b]88</B> GT and Formula. It was not standard or optional on any other year.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ahhh, well that would explain it.  Looks like I'll have to buy one  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Thanks for the info <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||gt boy||08-02-2001||11:26 PM||||how much difference does the rear sway bar make???||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||08-02-2001||11:32 PM||||Can I take a rear sway bar from a 88GT and just PUT it on a 87GT?||||reg||1
Z||000005||rodmcneill||08-03-2001||03:25 AM||||Rear sway bar makes a big difference to the handling, one of the best bang for the bucks. 88 rear sway bar is completely diff. from earlier models. I have heard of people using a 84-87 front sway bar in the rear of 84-87. I bought H.D. front and rear bars for my 86 GT from the Fiero Store, they come with poly. bushings and end links.||||reg||1
